# Saveable and Editable Authoring

- Every feature, UI element, animation, balance value, destination, timing, color, asset, and layout introduced or changed must be editable through a real saved Unity asset, prefab, scene object, ScriptableObject, or serialized Inspector field.
- Edit-time visuals must be genuine serialized prefab or scene children and must be the same objects used at runtime.
- Never present temporary, generated, hidden, `DontSave`, or runtime-only objects as editable authoring content.
- Runtime construction is allowed only as a defensive fallback or when explicitly requested; it must not replace the editable authored version.
- Direct edits made in Prefab Mode or the scene must persist after Save, domain reload, Play Mode, and reopening Unity.
- Runtime code must bind to and preserve authored transforms, colors, sprites, fonts, and component settings instead of silently rebuilding or overwriting them.
- Before handoff, verify persistence as well as runtime behavior. If a value cannot reasonably be exposed, explain why before implementing it.
